---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
The client-side search index. `strip_html` then `normalize_whitespace` turns each
rendered page into one flat string the browser can substring-match; jsonify does
the escaping. It reads each page's rendered HTML, so _plugins/search_index.rb renders
it after every page. The whole site's prose is a few hundred KB, fetched only when
someone actually opens search.
{%- endcomment -%}
[
{%- assign pages = site.html_pages | where_exp: "p", "p.title" -%}
{%- for p in pages -%}
{
  "title": {{ p.heading | default: p.title | jsonify }},
  "url": {{ p.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
  "description": {{ p.description | default: "" | jsonify }},
  "content": {{ p.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | jsonify }}
}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
